{"metadata":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"TensorProductView","kind":"identifier"}],"externalID":"s:13GraphProducts17TensorProductViewV","symbolKind":"struct","role":"symbol","title":"TensorProductView","modules":[{"name":"GraphProducts"}],"remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/GraphProducts\/TensorProductView.swift#L41","fileName":"TensorProductView.swift"},"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"TensorProductView","kind":"identifier"}],"roleHeading":"Structure"},"sections":[],"relationshipsSections":[{"title":"Conforms To","type":"conformsTo","kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/BidirectionalDirectedGraph","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","doc:\/\/GraphProducts\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/GraphProducts\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/GraphProducts\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/GraphProducts\/s16SendableMetatypeP"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@frozen"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"TensorProductView"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"First"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Second"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Vertices and their indices are as in "},{"code":"CartesianProductView","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". The row of (g, h) lists "},{"code":"(g′, h′)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"each entry g′ of G’s row of g and each entry h′ of H’s row of h, G outer. Rows are computed from"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the factors’ index rows and never hash."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An edge’s position is "},{"code":"Position(first: e, second: f, reversed:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":": G’s edge "},{"code":"e","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and H’s edge"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"f","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". In an undirected product two non-loop edges {a, b} and {c, d} give two edges, the straight"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"{(a, c), (b, d)} and the reversed {(a, d), (b, c)}, where a, c are the edges’ "},{"code":"u","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" ends; when"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"either is a self-loop they coincide and there is one, not reversed. A row lists a factor"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"self-loop from its first appearance only, so every product edge has each of its ends once in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the rows. Directed, "},{"code":"reversed","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is always false, and the product has edge indices"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"index(e)·m_H + index(f)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" when both factors have them; undirected it has none, because a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"self-loop changes how many edges a factor pair gives."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"abstract":[{"text":"The tensor product G × H of two graphs, both directed or both undirected, as a lazy view. Made","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"by ","type":"text"},{"code":"tensorProductView(_:_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Also called the direct, categorical or Kronecker product.","type":"text"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/GraphProducts\/documentation\/GraphProducts\/Tenso